# CodeIgniter 4 & PHP Standards

This is a **CodeIgniter 4** API backend (PHP ^8.1). Follow CI4 conventions and modern PHP best practices.

## PHP Standards

- Target **PHP 8.1+** features: typed properties, union types, `readonly`, enums where appropriate.
- Add `declare(strict_types=1);` at the top of **new** application files (`app/`).
- Use **type hints** on all method parameters and **return types** on all methods (including `void`).
- Use **property types** on class properties; avoid untyped `$model`-style properties when the type is known.
- Follow **PSR-12** formatting: 4-space indent, one class per file, `declare`/`namespace`/`use` order.
- Prefer early returns; avoid deep nesting.
- Catch specific exceptions; never use empty `catch` blocks.

## Project Structure

| Layer | Location | Base class |
|-------|----------|------------|
| Controllers | `app/Controllers/` | `BaseController` |
| Models | `app/Models/` | `BaseModel` |
| Migrations | `app/Database/Migrations/` | `Migration` |
| Config | `app/Config/` | — |
| Helpers | `app/Helpers/` | — |

- Namespace: `App\Controllers`, `App\Models`, `App\Database\Migrations`.
- Do not modify framework files in `vendor/`.

## Controllers

- Extend `BaseController`; use `ResponseTrait` for JSON API responses.
- Reuse shared CRUD logic via `baseIndex()`, `baseCreate()`, `baseUpdate()`, `baseDelete()` when applicable.
- Set `$this->model` in constructor or `initController` before calling base methods.
- Return typed responses: `ResponseInterface` from CI4 helpers, or `array`/`int|null` from base helpers.
- Validate input with `$this->validate($rules)` and return `$this->validator->getErrors()` on failure.
- Read JSON body with `$this->request->getJSON(true)`; query params with `$this->request->getVar()`.
- Use `auth()->user()` (CodeIgniter Shield) for authenticated user context.
- Register routes in `app/Config/Routes.php` using `$routes->group()` with appropriate filters (`cors`, `jwt`).

## Models

- Extend `BaseModel` (provides soft deletes, timestamps, validation scaffolding).
- Declare `$table`, `$allowedFields`, `$validationRules`, and `$validationMessages`.
- Keep database logic in models; keep controllers thin.
- Use Query Builder via model methods; avoid raw SQL unless necessary.

## Services & Dependencies

- Resolve framework services via `service('name')` or `config('Name')`.
- Inject dependencies through constructor when a class owns a specific model/service.
- Use `helper('name')` or declare in `$helpers` on the controller.

## Security

- Never commit secrets; use `.env` and `getenv()` / `env()`.
- Apply JWT filter on protected API route groups.
- Sanitize/validate all external input before persistence.
